      "problem": "Solve $f(x)=0,$ where $f(x) = \\dfrac{x^2-4x}{x^2+5x+6}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor $f(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-4x}{{x}^{2}+5x+6} \\\\  & =\\frac{x(x-4)}{(x+2)(x+3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(x-4) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions to $f(x)=0$ are $x=0$ and $x=4.$",
